Skia on Kosmos (docs/w5.md W5e). WebKit's copy of Skia asks for
Fontconfig everywhere but Windows and the PlayStation, and opens GL through
EGL or libepoxy. Kosmos has neither yet: its fonts are files in a folder,
found by Skia's own manager for one (SkFontMgr_custom_directory) over the
same FreeType everything else draws with, and Ganesh finds GL through
EGL - the EGL Kit's, which has no display (docs/w6.md W6b), so it is given
no functions and WebKit paints on the processor - until a GL or Vulkan
driver exists. The reference on this Mac takes the interface that finds
no native GL.

It is built as Unix (SK_BUILD_FOR_UNIX), which it otherwise takes for a
Mac, with FreeType's version the one it was built as. And five of its
files use streams, which Kosmos's libc++ is built without: where
_LIBCPP_HAS_LOCALIZATION is 0 they print with snprintf's %g and read with
strtod - what a stream in the C locale does - and are unchanged elsewhere.
And two files the list of sources leaves out are added: SkOSPath, which
the folder's manager uses, and SkStrikeRef, which SkFont does.

The same choices but Unix are made on this Mac with KOSMOS_SKIA_REFERENCE,
for the reference Kosmos's Skia is held to.

